# .cursorrules — Motivation Engine
# Place in the repo root as `.cursorrules`.
# This is the project constitution for the AI assistant. Rules are not negotiable
# within a task — if a rule gets in the way, that's a reason for a decisions.json
# entry, not for a workaround.

## What this project is
Motivation Engine — Ventora's knowledge layer: an ontology of human motivation
mechanisms (science → mechanisms → interface implementations) + the Control Center
showcase. Current stage: PHASE 2 — shelves, showcase, and tools-level source
fetching from a whitelist of public APIs. NO engine, NO LLM calls, NO database.

## Architectural invariants (violation = stop and ask the owner)
1. SOURCE OF TRUTH — files in the repo. Data lives ONLY in:
 /registry/**.json, /sources/sources.json, /decisions/decisions.json,
 /dossiers/**, /docs/**.md, /segments/segments.yaml (product-segment axis,
 D-047), /corpora/_ops/**.json (operational config).
   No data inside components, no databases. Knowledge files (registry,
   dossiers, docs, sources, decisions) are edited ONLY in git; the app has a
   NARROW write surface limited to /corpora/_ops/** and append-only auto-
   entries in decisions.json (D-023).
2. HONEST STATUSES — statuses in the showcase are COMPUTED from data.
   Hardcoding a status ("live", "connected", coverage numbers) in JSX/TS is
   forbidden. No data → show an honest empty state explaining what will appear
   here and when.
3. /cards/ is generated output only. Never create or edit by hand; it changes
   via render-cards.ts from the registry.
4. A mechanism record missing `metrics` or `constraints.hard_rules` is invalid.
   The validator must reject it. Do not weaken the schema for convenience.
5. NO premature infrastructure: do not add Postgres, Redis, queues, vector
   databases, microservices, docker-compose. Escalation triggers are described
   in docs/architecture.md — until they fire, the baseline stays file-based.
6. AUTH — single password: middleware + httpOnly HMAC cookie + ACCESS_PASSWORD
   from env. Do not add: accounts, roles, OAuth, magic links, session DBs,
   analytics, trackers.
7. Every architectural decision (stack, data structure, deviation from the plan)
   gets an entry in decisions.json (id D-XXX, date, essence, rationale) in the
   same PR.

## Content rules (critical)
8. DO NOT INVENT SCIENCE OR MECHANISMS. Cursor writes code, schemas, UI. The
   content of mechanisms, evidence grades, scientific claims, and dossier texts
   are entered only by the owner (Igor) or arrive from the future derivation
   pipeline. If a record example is needed for layout work — use the existing
   LA-01, do not generate new "plausible" mechanisms.
9. Seed mechanisms (11 items) have lifecycle_status: "candidate" and contain
   only: id, name, grade (draft), oneliner, parent. Do not flesh them out.
10. Language: everything is in English — data content, UI copy, documents, code,
    identifiers, commits.

## Stack and code conventions
11. Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript strict + Tailwind. Server Components by
    default; client components only where interactivity is required.
12. Data reading in the app: fs in server components / static generation. The
    Next.js app remains file-based — no runtime external fetches from app/
    (including middleware and server actions), with ONE exception (D-023):
    server actions under app/ops/ MAY call api.github.com to commit the
    allowlisted /corpora/_ops/** write surface, to dispatch harvest workflows
    (workflow_dispatch), to poll a run, and to download a run's quote artifact
    — nothing else, and harvesting itself never runs in the app. Scripts under
    tools/ MAY call ONLY these public APIs: api.openalex.org,
    api.semanticscholar.org, PubMed E-utilities (eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov),
    web.archive.org (CDX API). Any other external endpoint requires a new
    decisions.json entry first. LLM API calls remain forbidden everywhere in
    this repo.
13. Data types are generated from JSON schemas (or declared in /lib/types.ts
    mirroring the schemas). `any` is forbidden.
14. Design tokens — from the Control Center v0.1 reference: dark background
    #0E1512, panels #151F1A, emerald accent #34D399, statuses: live=emerald,
    wip=amber #E4B54E, plan=#7C93A8. Fonts: Space Grotesk (display), Inter
    (body), JetBrains Mono (data, ids, statuses). Do not invent a new palette.
15. Every screen must have a designed empty state (what will appear here, from
    which file/pipeline, and when).
16. Commits: conventional commits (feat:, fix:, data:, docs:, chore:).
    Changes to /registry, /sources, /decisions use the data: prefix.

## Definition of Done for any task
- npm run validate — green
- npm run build — no errors, no type warnings
- No status in the showcase is hardcoded (grep check for status string literals
  in app/)
- If the data structure changed — schema updated, validator updated, and a
  decisions.json entry added

## Never do at the current stage (Phase 2)
- Do not connect LLM APIs (OpenRouter/Anthropic/OpenAI) — there is no engine yet
- Do not build general scrapers; source connectors are allowed ONLY as scripts
  under tools/ calling the whitelisted APIs in rule 12
- Do not build data-editing forms in the UI for KNOWLEDGE (registry, dossiers,
  docs, sources, decisions) — that is edited in git. The ONLY UI write surface
  is operational config under /corpora/_ops/** and run triggering (D-023)
- Do not add dependencies "for the future"
